pass-sdfgiVoxelize = Draws the scene's meshes three times, once along each axis, with an orthographic camera over the dirty region and no attachment it writes: each fragment stores its voxel's albedo and emission and ORs its facing bit into the working images.
pass-sdfgiScroll = After a scroll, puts each kept solid cell of the cascade's old list back into the working images at its new position (one thread per old cell, an indirect dispatch sized by the old list).
pass-sdfgiScrollOcclusion = After a scroll, unpacks the kept part of the cascade's 4-bit occlusion into the eight working occlusion images, shifted by the scroll.
pass-sdfgiProbeScroll = After a scroll, copies each kept probe's 30 history slots and its average into the scratch textures at its new place, and seeds each new probe from the eight nearest probes of the coarser cascade.
pass-sdfgiProbeScrollStore = Copies the scrolled probe history and averages back from the scratch textures into the cascade's own.
pass-sdfgiProbeStoreScroll = After a scroll, converts the scrolled probes' averages into their octahedral maps again, so this frame's light pass bounces scrolled probes.
pass-sdfgiJumpFloodInit = Starts the half-size jump flood: each half-size cell takes one solid voxel of its 2 x 2 x 2 block as its seed, or none.
pass-sdfgiJumpFlood = A half-size jump-flood step with a large stride: each cell reads the seeds of its 26 neighbours a stride away and keeps the nearest.
pass-sdfgiJumpFloodShared = A jump-flood step with a small stride: a workgroup loads a 10 x 10 x 10 lattice of seeds a stride apart into shared memory once, and each cell picks the nearest of its 27 from there.
pass-sdfgiUpscale = Brings the half-size seeds back to full size: a solid voxel seeds itself, any other takes its half cell's seed and checks the voxels of that seed's block.
pass-sdfgiJumpFloodFull = One full-size jump-flood step with stride 1, which repairs what the half-size flood got wrong.
pass-sdfgiOcclusion = For one of the eight parity classes of probes, one workgroup per probe: spreads visibility from the probe through its 16 x 16 x 16 cells, shell by shell, with a barrier after each of the 22 shells.
pass-sdfgiStore = Writes the cascade's distance field (one byte a cell), packs the eight occlusion values of each cell into 4 bits each, and compacts the solid cells into the cascade's list with two levels of atomics, writing the next dispatch's size as it goes.
pass-sdfgiStaticLight = Adds the static lights once to every solid cell of a rebuilt cascade, storing the result in the cell's record of the list.
pass-sdfgiDynamicLight = One thread per solid cell of a quarter of the list each frame: adds the bounce from last frame's probes and every dynamic light (an SDF shadow march each), and writes the cell's light and its empty neighbours' into the cascade's light textures.
pass-sdfgiProbeProcess = One thread per probe of each cascade: traces this frame's rays through the distance fields, adds their light into 16 spherical-harmonic coefficients, and replaces the oldest of the 30 history slots in the exact integer sum.
pass-sdfgiProbeStore = One thread per map texel: evaluates each probe's averaged coefficients at its direction for irradiance and radiance, and writes them as shared-exponent words into the octahedral maps with their borders.
controls-gi_half_resolution = use_half_resolution
help-giHalfResolution = rendering/global_illumination/gi/use_half_resolution: the screen gather writes half-size buffers, one pixel of each 2 × 2 block, and the opaque pass reads them bilinearly, with no regard for depth: light bleeds across edges.
pass-sdfgiPrepassFS = The depth pre-pass, which also writes Godot's normal-roughness buffer: each pixel's normal and roughness, for the screen gather.
pass-sdfgiGatherCS = The screen gather, one thread per pixel in 8 x 8 workgroups: from the depth and the normal-roughness buffer, the pixel's position and normal; from the probes around it, its ambient and reflection, written into two RGBA16F buffers.

